<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#supreme-leader-of-iran">Glossary</a> · Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Supreme Leader of Iran</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1979–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Supreme Leader of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> is the highest office of the Islamic Republic of Iran, created by the constitution of 1979 on the principle of the guardianship of the Islamic jurist. Held first by Ayatollah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhollah-khomeini">Ruhollah Khomeini</a> and from 1989 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-khamenei">Ali Khamenei</a>, it commands the armed forces, appoints the heads of the judiciary and state broadcasting, and stands above the elected president and parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/supreme-leader-of-iran.jpg" alt="Supreme Leader of Iran" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Madden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_Iran.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
